/*
Instructions:
------------
1) Prereqs: Your control in PD should _at least_ have the following entries in AMD Dependencies:
- com.ibm.bpm.coach.controls/utilities --> utilities
- com.ibm.bpm.coach.controls/utilities --> bpmext
...Add more AMD dependencies to fit the needs of your control

2) Rename the function below from bpmext_control_InitButton to bpmext_control_Init<Your control name>,
for example: bpmext_control_InitDateTime

3) Change the function parameters to match the objects in your AMD Dependencies

4) Change the function call in the control's Inline Javascript section to match the function and
parameters specified below - for example from:
bpmext_control_InitButton.call(this, bpmext, utilities);
...to:
bpmext_control_InitDateTime.call(this, utilities, bpmext, domClass, domConstruct);
...note how the function is invoked using call(), and the "this", "utilities", and "bpmext"
parameters are always passed

General Notes:
-------------
The control logic below makes use of a _proto and an _instance object. They sort of work like
local namespaces to reduce the risk of name collision if IBM decides to add more functions and
attributes at the top level of their Coach View class
 */

